  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN213.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">piriviṭai vēṟupaṭṭa talaimakaḷait tōḻi vaṟpuṟuttiyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">How the confidante comforted HER who had undergone changes in the time of separation.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN213.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>viḷainal yāṉai viṟaṟpōrt toṇṭaiya</l>
        <l>riḷamaḻai tavaḻu mēṟṟaru neṭuṅkōṭ</l>
        <l>ṭōṅkuveḷ ḷaruvi vēṅkaṭat tumpark</l>
        <l>koykuḻai yatiral vaikupular vāṅkiya</l>
        <l><anchor n="2"/>curiyirum pittai curumpupaṭac cūṭi</l>
        <l>yikaṉmuṉait taḻīiya vēṟuṭaip perunirai</l>
        <l>naṉaimutir naṟavi ṉāṭpali koṭukkum</l>
        <l>vāṉiṇap pukaviṉ vaṭukar tēettu</l>
        <l>niḻalkavi ṉiḻanta nī<supplied>ri</supplied> ṉīḷiṭai</l>
        <l>yaḻalavi <supplied>ra</supplied>ruñcura neṭiya veṉṉā</l>
        <l>kālā yantaṇa rāyiṉum pakalcelap </l>
        <l>palkatir vāṅkiya paṭucuṭa ramaiyattup</l>
        <l>perumaraṅ koṉṟa cālpuku viyaṉpuṉat</l>
        <l>terimaruḷ katira <supplied>tiru</supplied>maṇi yimaikkum</l>
        <l>velpōr vāṉavaṉ kollik kuṭavarai</l>
        <l>vēyoḻuk kaṉṉa cāyiṟaip paṇaittōṭ</l>
        <l>peruṅkaviṉ citaiya nīṅki yāṉṟō </l>
        <l>rarumpeṟa lulaka mamiḻtoṭu peṟiṉuñ</l>
        <l>ceṉṟutā nīṭalō vilarē yeṉṟuṅ</l>
        <l>kalampeyak kaviḻnta kaḻaṟoṭit taṭakkai</l>
        <l>valampaṭu veṉṟi vāyvāṭ cōḻa</l>
        <l>rilaṅkunīrk kāviri yiḻipuṉal varitta</l>
        <l>vaṟaleṉa neṟitta kūnta </l>
        <l>luṟaliṉ cāyalō ṭoṉṟutaṉ maṟantē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="11c">Even though, (11c)</l>
        <l corresp="3">beyond Vēṅkaṭam with white waterfalls high</l>
        <l corresp="2">on tall peaks difficult to climb that are covered with young clouds</l>
        <l corresp="1">[belonging to] the Toṇṭaiyar of victorious battle with mature good elephants,</l>
        <l corresp="8">in the land of the Vaṭukar with food of pure fat,</l>
        <l>where they wear what they pull from the wild jasmine with plucked sprouts when it dawns</l>
        <l corresp="4f">on [their] curly dark hair tufts so that bees descend [on them</l>
        <l corresp="7">and] give daily offerings of toddy matured with buds</l>
        <l corresp="6">for the large herds with bulls that were apprehended on the enemy frontier,</l>
        <l>there being a time when he did not say that in the difficult desert shining with fires</l>
        <l corresp="9-11a">the waterless roads were long that lost the beauty of shade,</l>
        <l rend="indent3" corresp="11b 18d">he is a brahmin, even if,</l>
        <l corresp="17a-c">having left [you] so that [your] great beauty is spoiled</l>
        <l corresp="16">in [your] bamboo shoulders with joints flexible like the movements of bamboo</l>
        <l corresp="15">on the western mountain of Kolli, [belonging to] him of the sky (~the Cēra), of victorious battle,</l>
        <l corresp="14">where brilliant gems twinkle with flame-like rays</l>
        <l corresp="13">in the vast fields that yield plenty where the big trees were felled</l>
        <l corresp="11d-12">at the moment of sunset when [the sun] retracts [its] many rays, as the day goes,</l>
        <l corresp="17d-18">he were to obtain the difficult-to-obtain world of the noble ones along with ambrosia,</l>
        <l corresp="19">as for his going [on and] delaying, not he – for ever</l>
        <l corresp="24">forgetting [how] to be one with [your] grace, pleasing to experience.</l>
        <l corresp="23">[your] tresses that are curved like the black sand</l>
        <l corresp="22">that is lined by the descending flood of the Kāviri with shining water,</l>
        <l corresp="21">[belonging to] the Cōḻa whose sword has a victorious blade,</l>
        <l corresp="20">[his] broad hands with loosening  armlets that turn over when he showers [gift] ornaments.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
